From 0fe871f38aac7ca6bdfebf66f8a0070185711538 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sunny <213254234@seu.edu.cn>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 17:12:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Add \examanswerspace; fix misleading documentation on [..]
 argument

The examquestions environment's optional argument sets \parskip, which
only takes effect BETWEEN paragraphs. Using it for answer space therefore
produces two counter-intuitive results:
  1) the gap lands BEFORE the first question (the newline/indent at the
     start of the environment body forms an empty paragraph)
  2) the LAST question gets no space (no following paragraph, so the
     skip is discarded at the end of the document)

Changes:
- exampaper.cls: add \examanswerspace{<length>} (\par\vspace{#1}) for
  explicit per-question answer space that also works on the last question
- README.md: correct the four places describing [7cm] as answer space;
  add the pitfall to the gotchas list; document the new command
- example-exam.tex: use [0pt] + \examanswerspace{7cm}
- main.tex: update skeleton comments and the sample section
